Find patched threading without importing eventlet

oslo_messaging._utils imported eventlet and oslo.utils' eventletutils
only to learn whether threading was monkey patched. Nothing can be
patched before eventlet is imported, so look in sys.modules instead.
Services that patch first get the same unpatched threading and queue.

glance-api imports no eventlet or dns modules in a probe, and uses 84MB
of anonymous memory, not 93MB. This needs futurist's "Do not import
eventlet until it is needed" and oslo.utils' change to eventletutils as
well: with only some of the three, other imports bring eventlet back.

Prompt: Mikal asked for import-memory fixes that can be landed one at a
time and measured in devstack CI; oslo.messaging is one of several
importers of eventlet in the threaded API services.

